# Board/fixture YAML checks out with LF on EVERY platform.
#
# WINDOWS CI BREAK, run 30773825956 (job "pcb test (windows-latest)"): the
# GitHub Windows runner checks out with git's Windows default core.autocrlf,
# so committed *.yaml arrived as CRLF. Go's os.ReadFile is byte-exact (unlike
# Python's read_text(), which normalizes newlines and is why the worker's
# pytest suite stayed green), so a Go test mutating a fixture with an
# LF-terminated literal pattern silently matched NOTHING and exercised the
# UNMUTATED board — see TestPCBWorkerStdioSmoke_ExportAssembly in main_test.go
# and the fail-closed replaceOnceLF helper beside it. Pinning EOL here removes
# the platform difference at its source; the helper's no-op refusal is the
# belt to this file's braces.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
